**Status** Done on 2026-11-22. [Replay, screenshot and limits](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage03/README.md)

## Capability

Bind one existing canvas placement and Room to model handles and route normal selection, movement and undo through the bridge.

## Completion checks

- [x] Drag the existing item, undo and reopen it. Its Record binding and the other occurrence survive.

## Implementation references

[Durable model and accepted-change foundation](../features/Model.lingua) · [02.T03](../features/Model.lingua#task-02t03)

Use the applicable fixture, tolerances and recovery cases in [02 · Durable model](../contracts/Durable-model-contracts.lingua#concrete-acceptance-replay).

**Handoff** Open Edit → Workspaces → Scene document. Select a model occurrence, select an existing local Sand that belongs directly to a Room, then choose **Link selected Room member to this placement**. The scene root uses the Room’s frame. Its linked slot uses the Sand’s durable placement ID and preserves its Record UID. Selection works from the canvas and from the scene tree. A pointer release creates one local scene edit, and **Undo scene edit** restores the Sand and its inspector together.

The offscreen desktop replay moved the linked bracket from (5, 0, 1) to (5.8, 0, 1.32) m. One undo restored the original translation. After saving and restarting, both occurrences still shared their original definition. The binding resolved the same Room, existing Sand and Record. The optional `canvas-room/1` profile covers one ungrouped direct member in a local workspace. Run `cargo run --locked -p lince-sandbox --example workspace_scene -- <fresh-directory> --bridge` in the interface shell. Base revision `bee6f4cc6ea9`. [Replay, screenshot and limits](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage03/README.md)

**Laboratory showcase.** Select one model slot and the existing Bracket Sand, then choose **Link selected Room member to this placement**. Drag the Bracket while the physics playground runs. The cumulative replay checks that undo restores the Sand, redo changes only its slot, and a fresh desktop resolves the Room, Sand and Record after switching workspaces. [Showcase guide and cumulative replay](../../../fixtures/workspace/showcase/README.md)

